{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>In a pillar of cloud.</b> It came forth singular — not like the way of flesh and blood. A king of flesh and blood, when he goes out to war, goes out with multitudes, and when he goes out in peace, goes out with few. But the way of the Holy One, blessed be He: when He goes out to war, He goes out singular, as it says ״אִישׁ מִלְחָמָה״ (Exodus 15); and when He goes out in peace, He goes out with multitudes, as it says (Psalms 68) ״רֶכֶב אֱלֹהִים רִבֹּתַיִם אַלְפֵי שִׁנְאָן״ (Sifrei)." "<b>And He called Aaron and Miriam.</b> That they would be drawn out and go forth from the court to meet the Word." "<b>And the two of them went out.</b> And why did He draw them out and separate them from Moses? Because one states part of a person's praise to his face and all of it not in his presence. And so we find with Noah — not in his presence it says ״אִישׁ צַדִּיק תָּמִים״ (Genesis 6), and in his presence it says ״כִּי אֹתְךָ רָאִיתִי צַדִּיק לְפָנַי״ (ibid. 7). Another interpretation: so that He would not hear the rebuke of Aaron (Sifrei)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:35.249377112Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}